From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: libretro: the disk shader cache loads on a thread, with RetroArch's progress bar

A game whose shader cache another build made compiles every pipeline again when it
starts: 626 of them in Castlevania, about a minute on the RG52 Mini. The core did that
in context_reset, inside RetroArch's video init, so nothing was presented and the
screen stayed black as if the core had hung.

do_load_game now only marks the load as pending; the first retro_run starts it on a
thread (LoadDefaultDiskResources with its stop flag and progress callback) and, while
it runs, presents the last frame again with RetroArch's progress message
(SET_MESSAGE_EXT, type progress: "Compiling shaders: n / m" or "Loading shader cache"),
shown only once the load has taken a second. Emulation starts when it is done, as
before. A savestate RetroArch loads meanwhile (an entry state, -e) is kept and loaded
when the cache is done; none is made meanwhile (RetroArch's undo copy before it gets
none); unload and reset stop the load.

